      "writtenOn": "2021-12-02T00:03:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeh. The phoneId-\u003e subId conversion is ugly, even put into CarrierConfigLoader.\n\nCarrierConfigLoader is really phoneId based, almost no subId is involved. I felt putting the conversion there pollute this design. I prefer to keep it here since it is CarrierService API that require subId, not CarrierConfigLoader.\n\nAnother option is just let onLoadConfig accept slotIndex instead subId. Then we don\u0027t need this conversion. But this actually force the Carrier App facing the slotIndex instead of subId. And it is a bit inconsistent since the new version of notifyCarrierNetworkChange accept subId.\n\nLet\u0027s keep this open to see if any preferences from telephony team\u0027s review.",
      "parentUuid": "6b9e70c8_1cf8fce0",
